The base test passed (1 passed, 76 ignored — all good). The io build still fails: E0451 "fields `xs` and `inner` of struct `Reader` are private" — the `reader`/`writer` methods are in a separate `impl` block outside the `io` module, so they can't access the private fields of `Reader`/`Writer` (private fields are only visible within the module where they're defined and its child modules).

Fix: move the `reader`/`writer` methods into the `io` module as an `impl Xorcism` block, or make the fields `pub`. The cleanest is: define the constructor functions inside the `io` module. Let's restructure:

```rust
#[cfg(feature = "io")]
pub mod io {
    use std::io::{self, Read, Write};

    use super::Xorcism;

    pub struct Reader<'a, R> {
        xs: Xorcism<'a>,
        inner: R,
    }

    impl<'a, R: Read> Read for Reader<'a, R> { ... }

    pub struct Writer<'a, W> {
        xs: Xorcism<'a>,
        inner: W,
    }

    impl<'a, W: Write> Write for Writer<'a, W> { ... }

    impl<'a> Xorcism<'a> {
        pub fn reader<R: Read>(self, reader: R) -> Reader<'a, R> {
            Reader { xs: self, inner: reader }
        }

        pub fn writer<W: Write>(self, writer: W) -> Writer<'a, W> {
            Writer { xs: self, inner: writer }
        }
    }
}
